1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,280
Hello everyone, and welcome to Two Cups English.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:06,720
I'm Mia, and Ben is here with me.

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:09,560
This podcast is for people who are learning English.

4
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:11,060
We speak slowly.

5
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:12,980
We use simple words.

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:16,400
And we repeat the important words many times.

7
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:19,920
Today, our topic is slow days.

8
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,580
A slow day is a day with no plan.

9
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:24,830
A day with nothing.

10
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,250
Ben, how was your Sunday?

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:28,820
Hi Mia.

12
00:00:28,840 --> 00:00:29,340
Hi everyone.

13
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,200
My Sunday was very slow.

14
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:34,680
I stayed in bed until ten.

15
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,320
I did not cook.

16
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:37,880
I did not clean.

17
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:41,160
I just looked at the window and drank my coffee.

18
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:44,540
For the first hour, I felt great.

19
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:52,680
But then a small voice said, "Ben, you are wasting the day." Do you know that voice, Mia?

20
00:00:53,660 --> 00:00:56,020
Oh, I know that voice very well, Ben.

21
00:00:56,520 --> 00:00:58,640
It talks to me every weekend.

22
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:00,320
It says, "Do something.

23
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:01,320
Be useful.

24
00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:04,860
Other people are busy." And I feel bad.

25
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:07,039
On a free day, I feel bad.

26
00:01:07,720 --> 00:01:08,700
That is strange, right?

27
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:11,720
We work all week, and then we cannot rest.

28
00:01:12,580 --> 00:01:14,520
Yes, that is very strange, Mia.

29
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:17,760
So what do you do when the voice comes?

30
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:19,540
Do you get up and work?

31
00:01:20,140 --> 00:01:21,240
Or do you stay in bed?

32
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:23,680
Sometimes I get up.

33
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:26,440
I do many small things, and I feel tired at night.

34
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:28,240
But sometimes I stay.

35
00:01:28,910 --> 00:01:31,180
And that is the day I want to talk about today.

36
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:32,540
A slow day.

37
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:33,940
A day with nothing.

38
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:35,980
And why it is okay.

39
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:37,620
I like that, Mia.

40
00:01:38,210 --> 00:01:42,680
"It is okay." I think many people need to hear those words.

41
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,180
So here is our plan for today.

42
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:49,280
In part one, we talk about our own slow days.

43
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:51,900
What we do, and what we feel.

44
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:56,400
In part two, we ask why a slow day is okay.

45
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:58,920
And I have a true story for that.

46
00:02:00,220 --> 00:02:03,720
In part three, we share simple ideas for a slow day.

47
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:05,240
Does that sound good?

48
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,080
That sounds good, Ben.

49
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:11,070
And to everyone listening, please do not worry if you miss something.

50
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:13,040
You will hear it again.

51
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:17,800
You can listen while you cook, while you walk, or while you rest.

52
00:02:17,820 --> 00:02:19,400
Yes, you can rest and listen.

53
00:02:19,780 --> 00:02:20,500
That is allowed.

54
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:21,920
Okay, Ben.

55
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:22,640
Part one.

56
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,400
Tell me about your slow day.

57
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:25,740
Start from the morning.

58
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:27,880
Okay, part one.

59
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:30,170
My slow day starts late.

60
00:02:31,180 --> 00:02:32,340
I do not set an alarm.

61
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:34,900
I wake up when my body wakes up.

62
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:37,680
Last Sunday, that was nine thirty.

63
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:39,840
I stayed in bed for a while.

64
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:41,780
I did not look at my phone.

65
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:45,020
I looked at the light on the wall.

66
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:47,060
Then I got up, and I made coffee.

67
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:48,620
Slowly.

68
00:02:49,489 --> 00:02:50,329
I did not hurry.

69
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,000
And I sat by the window with my cup.

70
00:02:54,080 --> 00:02:55,040
I love that, Ben.

71
00:02:55,710 --> 00:02:59,780
"I wake up when my body wakes up." That is a beautiful sentence.

72
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:02,680
My slow day is a little different.

73
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:05,400
I wake up early, even on a slow day.

74
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,160
My body is used to it.

75
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,280
But I do not get up.

76
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:09,900
I stay under the blanket.

77
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,940
I listen to the sounds outside.

78
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:13,180
Birds.

79
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:14,020
A car.

80
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:15,840
Rain, if I am lucky.

81
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:17,900
I love rain on a slow day.

82
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,440
Rain is perfect for a slow day, Mia.

83
00:03:21,900 --> 00:03:24,459
Nobody says, "Why are you inside?" when it rains.

84
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,020
So you stay in bed.

85
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:27,390
What comes next?

86
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:28,720
Do you eat breakfast?

87
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:31,740
Yes, Ben, but a slow breakfast.

88
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,899
Not toast standing in the kitchen.

89
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:35,400
I sit down.

90
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:36,680
I make tea.

91
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:40,000
I put butter on the bread, and I eat slowly.

92
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:41,920
Sometimes I read a little.

93
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:43,800
Sometimes I read nothing.

94
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:45,520
I just look at my cup.

95
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,920
Twenty minutes for breakfast.

96
00:03:48,660 --> 00:03:50,719
On a work day, it is three minutes.

97
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:53,000
Three minutes on a work day.

98
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:54,480
Twenty minutes on a slow day.

99
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:56,460
That is a big difference, Mia.

100
00:03:57,090 --> 00:03:58,940
And I think the difference is not the food.

101
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:00,820
The food is the same.

102
00:04:00,860 --> 00:04:02,520
Bread and tea.

103
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:04,640
The difference is the time.

104
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:07,580
On a slow day, we give time to small things.

105
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,160
Exactly, Ben.

106
00:04:09,740 --> 00:04:11,470
We give time to small things.

107
00:04:12,700 --> 00:04:16,740
So after your coffee by the window, what do you do?

108
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:17,960
Or do you do nothing?

109
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:20,160
Mostly nothing, Mia.

110
00:04:20,570 --> 00:04:21,800
And that is hard for me.

111
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:24,600
After coffee, I feel the voice coming.

112
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:29,100
"Ben, do something." So I do one small thing.

113
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,700
I water the plants.

114
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:32,420
It takes five minutes.

115
00:04:33,020 --> 00:04:34,080
Then I sit again.

116
00:04:34,740 --> 00:04:35,940
Maybe I play some music.

117
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:37,040
Old songs.

118
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,020
And I listen to the whole song.

119
00:04:39,590 --> 00:04:40,500
Not while I work.

120
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:41,600
Just listen.

121
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,780
Listening to a whole song.

122
00:04:44,420 --> 00:04:46,320
Ben, that is so rare now.

123
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:49,180
I always play music while I do something else.

124
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:50,340
Cooking.

125
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:51,220
Cleaning.

126
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,180
Writing messages.

127
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:54,620
I never just listen.

128
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:58,280
On my next slow day, I want to try that.

129
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:00,290
One song, and nothing else.

130
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:01,960
Try it, Mia.

131
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,260
It feels strange at first.

132
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,030
Your hands want to do something.

133
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:08,200
But after one minute, you relax.

134
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:09,880
Now, what about the afternoon?

135
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:13,400
For me, the afternoon is the hard part of a slow day.

136
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:14,460
What about you?

137
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,660
The afternoon is hard for me too, Ben.

138
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,680
In the morning, a slow day feels good.

139
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:24,060
But at two o'clock, the voice gets loud.

140
00:05:24,790 --> 00:05:25,960
"Half the day is gone.

141
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:29,130
You did nothing." So I do this.

142
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:30,630
I go for a walk.

143
00:05:31,420 --> 00:05:32,440
Not a fast walk.

144
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,060
A slow walk.

145
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:36,440
I do not go anywhere.

146
00:05:36,560 --> 00:05:39,220
I just walk around my street and come back.

147
00:05:39,320 --> 00:05:40,980
A walk with no place to go.

148
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,460
I like that, Mia.

149
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:44,740
Most walks have a goal.

150
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:45,820
The shop.

151
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:46,700
The bus.

152
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:47,580
Work.

153
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,940
But a slow walk has no goal.

154
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:51,600
The walk is the goal.

155
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,360
How long do you walk?

156
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:55,280
Maybe thirty minutes, Ben.

157
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,400
Sometimes I sit on a bench.

158
00:05:58,040 --> 00:05:58,800
I watch people.

159
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:00,760
A child with a dog.

160
00:06:01,140 --> 00:06:02,460
An old man with bread.

161
00:06:03,220 --> 00:06:04,140
Nobody knows me.

162
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:05,720
Nobody needs me.

163
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:07,459
And that feels good.

164
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:10,940
Then I go home, and I feel a little lighter.

165
00:06:11,490 --> 00:06:15,780
"Nobody needs me, and that feels good." That is honest, Mia.

166
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,640
I think many people feel that.

167
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:20,260
All week, everyone needs us.

168
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:21,360
Our boss.

169
00:06:21,940 --> 00:06:23,120
Our family.

170
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:24,640
Our phone.

171
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:27,640
On a slow day, nobody needs us for a few hours.

172
00:06:28,220 --> 00:06:29,440
And that is not lonely.

173
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:31,040
That is rest.

174
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,300
Yes, Ben.

175
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:33,860
That is rest.

176
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:36,420
And what is your afternoon like?

177
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:37,910
Do you also go out?

178
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:39,700
Not always, Mia.

179
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:41,060
Sometimes I take a nap.

180
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:42,820
A real nap.

181
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,820
On the sofa, with a blanket.

182
00:06:44,860 --> 00:06:46,840
Twenty minutes, maybe thirty.

183
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:50,220
When I was younger, I thought naps were for children and old people.

184
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,620
Now I think naps are for tired people.

185
00:06:53,260 --> 00:06:55,220
And I am a tired person on Sunday.

186
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:58,820
We are all tired people on Sunday, Ben.

187
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:02,420
I think a nap is a very good slow day thing.

188
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:04,600
Do you feel bad after the nap?

189
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:05,480
Or good?

190
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,600
For one minute, I feel bad.

191
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:14,620
I wake up and think, "Oh no, I slept." But then I stand up, I drink water, and I feel new.

192
00:07:14,660 --> 00:07:16,729
Like a small new morning in the afternoon.

193
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:18,660
So the nap is good.

194
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:19,840
The voice is wrong.

195
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,040
Ben, can I ask something?

196
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:23,580
Do you live alone?

197
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:26,020
Because a slow day alone is easy.

198
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:28,620
But a slow day with other people is different.

199
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,420
Good question, Mia.

200
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:31,460
I live with my brother.

201
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:33,240
And yes, it is different.

202
00:07:33,920 --> 00:07:35,960
On my slow day, he wants to talk.

203
00:07:36,380 --> 00:07:37,300
He wants to go out.

204
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:39,160
He wants to fix the bike.

205
00:07:40,080 --> 00:07:41,520
And I say, "Not today.

206
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:45,400
Today I rest." At first, he did not understand.

207
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:46,540
Now he knows.

208
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,520
Sunday is my slow day.

209
00:07:48,790 --> 00:07:50,600
And sometimes, he rests too.

210
00:07:51,390 --> 00:07:53,700
We sit in the same room and do nothing together.

211
00:07:54,420 --> 00:07:56,040
Doing nothing together.

212
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,220
I like that a lot, Ben.

213
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:59,660
My sister has two small children.

214
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:02,480
She says a slow day is impossible for her.

215
00:08:02,870 --> 00:08:04,160
The children never stop.

216
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,540
But last month, she tried something.

217
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,840
She told the children, "Today is a slow day.

218
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:10,920
We stay home.

219
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:14,080
We do nothing." And the children loved it.

220
00:08:14,140 --> 00:08:15,680
They built a house with blankets.

221
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,480
They rested in the house all afternoon.

222
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:20,160
A blanket house.

223
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,280
That is the perfect slow day, Mia.

224
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,240
Children know how to rest.

225
00:08:24,630 --> 00:08:25,800
They do not feel guilty.

226
00:08:26,290 --> 00:08:27,560
They do not hear the voice.

227
00:08:27,960 --> 00:08:29,590
They just stop when they are tired.

228
00:08:30,390 --> 00:08:31,340
We can learn from them.

229
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,460
Nothing is okay for a child.

230
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:35,640
So nothing is okay for us.

231
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,220
The voice is wrong.

232
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,240
I want to remember that, Ben.

233
00:08:39,980 --> 00:08:40,660
And the evening?

234
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:42,580
How does your slow day end?

235
00:08:43,160 --> 00:08:44,940
My slow day ends early, Mia.

236
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,660
I cook something simple.

237
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:47,600
Eggs.

238
00:08:48,119 --> 00:08:48,460
Rice.

239
00:08:49,119 --> 00:08:49,420
Soup.

240
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:52,440
I eat at the table, not in front of the computer.

241
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:54,700
Then I wash the dishes slowly.

242
00:08:55,240 --> 00:08:56,460
Then I read a few pages.

243
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,120
And I go to bed at ten.

244
00:08:58,760 --> 00:08:59,640
No phone in bed.

245
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,960
And I sleep very well.

246
00:09:02,020 --> 00:09:03,280
Better than any other night.

247
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:05,140
That is a good evening, Ben.

248
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:06,760
My evening is similar.

249
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:08,620
But I have one more thing.

250
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:12,960
Before bed, I say to myself, "Today I did nothing.

251
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:15,980
And that is okay." I say it out loud.

252
00:09:16,020 --> 00:09:17,240
It sounds silly.

253
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:18,440
But it helps.

254
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:19,840
The voice is quiet after that.

255
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:22,100
That is not silly, Mia.

256
00:09:22,380 --> 00:09:23,100
That is smart.

257
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:24,540
You answer the voice.

258
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,020
Okay, so that was part one.

259
00:09:27,380 --> 00:09:28,140
Our slow days.

260
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:33,260
Late mornings, slow breakfast, a walk with no goal, a nap, a simple dinner.

261
00:09:33,730 --> 00:09:35,180
And a small sentence before bed.

262
00:09:36,040 --> 00:09:37,039
Now, part two.

263
00:09:37,860 --> 00:09:39,080
Why is a slow day okay?

264
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:42,060
Mia, do you want to start, or should I tell my story?

265
00:09:42,820 --> 00:09:43,900
Tell your story, Ben.

266
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:45,620
You said it is a true story.

267
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:46,760
I want to hear it.

268
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:49,060
Okay, part two.

269
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,140
This is a true story.

270
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:55,170
In 2019, a writer named Olga Mecking wrote an article for The New York Times.

271
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:56,860
She lives in the Netherlands.

272
00:09:57,460 --> 00:09:59,180
In the Netherlands, people have a word.

273
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:03,240
The word is "niksen." Niksen means doing nothing.

274
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:04,440
Not reading.

275
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:05,620
Not watching.

276
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:07,290
Not thinking about work.

277
00:10:07,840 --> 00:10:08,760
Just doing nothing.

278
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:09,700
Sitting.

279
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:11,220
Looking out of the window.

280
00:10:12,080 --> 00:10:13,600
A word for doing nothing?

281
00:10:14,040 --> 00:10:15,330
Ben, that is wonderful.

282
00:10:15,900 --> 00:10:17,680
In English, we do not have that word.

283
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:21,340
We only have "lazy." And lazy is a bad word.

284
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,640
Yes, Mia, and that was her point.

285
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:28,020
Olga wrote that in many countries, doing nothing feels bad.

286
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:29,460
We call it lazy.

287
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:30,740
We call it wasting time.

288
00:10:31,450 --> 00:10:33,500
But in the Netherlands, niksen is normal.

289
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:38,400
People say, "I am going to niksen for a while." And nobody feels bad.

290
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:41,140
The article became very popular.

291
00:10:41,210 --> 00:10:42,110
Many people read it.

292
00:10:42,900 --> 00:10:46,140
Later, in 2021, she wrote a book with the same name.

293
00:10:46,800 --> 00:10:48,120
Niksen.

294
00:10:48,280 --> 00:10:49,820
Many people read it.

295
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:56,700
So many people wanted to hear, "It is okay to do nothing." Ben, why do you think the article was so popular?

296
00:10:57,840 --> 00:11:00,160
I think because everyone is tired, Mia.

297
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:00,960
We work.

298
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:01,520
We study.

299
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:03,000
We look at our phones.

300
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,940
Even our free time is busy.

301
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:08,320
We watch a show, and we check messages at the same time.

302
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:13,670
So when someone says, "You can do nothing, and it is good for you," people feel relief.

303
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:16,230
Like a heavy bag coming off their shoulders.

304
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:19,380
A heavy bag coming off.

305
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:20,320
Yes, Ben.

306
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:21,860
I felt that when you said the word.

307
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:22,980
Niksen.

308
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:25,420
But let me ask a hard question.

309
00:11:26,080 --> 00:11:27,420
Is it really good for us?

310
00:11:27,940 --> 00:11:29,480
Or does it just feel good?

311
00:11:30,359 --> 00:11:31,160
Good question, Mia.

312
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,040
Olga wrote about that too.

313
00:11:33,780 --> 00:11:36,100
When we do nothing, our mind is not empty.

314
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:37,880
It is working quietly.

315
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:39,340
Ideas come.

316
00:11:39,900 --> 00:11:41,000
Problems get smaller.

317
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:45,890
Many people say, "I had my best idea in the shower." Why?

318
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,280
Because in the shower, we do nothing.

319
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:51,060
So a slow day is not empty.

320
00:11:51,100 --> 00:11:53,250
It is a quiet room where ideas can come in.

321
00:11:54,149 --> 00:11:56,340
A quiet room where ideas can come in.

322
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,880
Ben, I think that is true.

323
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:01,160
My best ideas never come at my desk.

324
00:12:01,630 --> 00:12:03,100
They come on my slow walk.

325
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:04,480
Or in the bath.

326
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:06,740
Or in bed, before sleep.

327
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:09,380
So the slow day is doing something.

328
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,640
It is just doing it quietly.

329
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,240
Exactly, Mia.

330
00:12:13,810 --> 00:12:15,020
And there is one more thing.

331
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:17,420
Rest is not a reward.

332
00:12:18,160 --> 00:12:20,420
Many people think, "First I work hard.

333
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:23,720
Then I can rest." But rest is not a prize.

334
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:27,300
Rest is a part of life, like food and water.

335
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:32,980
We do not say, "I worked hard, so now I can drink water." We just drink.

336
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:34,800
Rest should be the same.

337
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:40,020
"Rest is not a reward." Ben, I want to stop here for a moment.

338
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:42,840
Because I think this is the big idea of today.

339
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:45,420
I always thought rest was a prize.

340
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:47,680
Finish the list, then rest.

341
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,880
But the list never finishes.

342
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:51,200
So I never rest.

343
00:12:51,949 --> 00:12:54,820
And then Sunday comes, and I feel guilty.

344
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:55,720
Yes, Mia.

345
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:57,620
The list never finishes.

346
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:58,640
That is the trap.

347
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:02,350
If rest comes after the list, rest never comes.

348
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:05,500
So we need to put rest inside the day.

349
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,120
Not after.

350
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:08,300
Inside.

351
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:10,420
A slow day is a whole day of rest.

352
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:13,800
But even a small slow hour is good.

353
00:13:13,810 --> 00:13:16,480
Do you have small slow times in your week?

354
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:17,730
Not a whole day.

355
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,770
Just an hour?

356
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:22,010
Ben, I want to say one more thing about permission.

357
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:24,560
Some slow days are not nice.

358
00:13:25,380 --> 00:13:27,040
I rest, and I still feel bad.

359
00:13:27,840 --> 00:13:29,140
The voice does not stop.

360
00:13:29,940 --> 00:13:32,940
I look at the ceiling, and I feel empty, not calm.

361
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,140
Is that slow day still okay?

362
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:37,240
Yes, Mia.

363
00:13:37,320 --> 00:13:38,780
That slow day is still okay.

364
00:13:39,480 --> 00:13:41,180
Rest is not always a good feeling.

365
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:43,640
Sometimes rest is just stopping.

366
00:13:44,300 --> 00:13:45,660
Your body stops.

367
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:47,100
Your hands stop.

368
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,880
Even if your mind is loud, your body is resting.

369
00:13:50,590 --> 00:13:52,940
And the next day, your body says thank you.

370
00:13:53,580 --> 00:13:54,700
The feeling comes later.

371
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,240
Or it does not come.

372
00:13:56,800 --> 00:13:57,980
But the rest is real.

373
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:02,700
The rest is real, even when the feeling is not.

374
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:03,600
That helps me, Ben.

375
00:14:04,140 --> 00:14:06,540
Because I always wait for the calm feeling.

376
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:12,080
And when it does not come, I think, "I did it wrong." But there is no wrong way to rest.

377
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:15,380
A slow day is okay even when it is not perfect.

378
00:14:16,420 --> 00:14:17,840
Exactly, Mia.

379
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,320
There is no wrong way to rest.

380
00:14:19,900 --> 00:14:21,900
A perfect slow day is not the goal.

381
00:14:22,579 --> 00:14:23,840
A slow day is the goal.

382
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:25,720
Just a day with less.

383
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:27,080
Less noise.

384
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:28,200
Less work.

385
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:29,960
Less list.

386
00:14:30,030 --> 00:14:30,720
More nothing.

387
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:32,340
And nothing is okay.

388
00:14:33,620 --> 00:14:34,300
I think so, Ben.

389
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:36,700
Wednesday evening.

390
00:14:36,860 --> 00:14:39,020
I do not plan anything on Wednesday evening.

391
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:40,260
I come home.

392
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:41,380
I make tea.

393
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:42,480
I sit.

394
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:44,460
Sometimes I call my mother.

395
00:14:45,260 --> 00:14:46,400
Sometimes I do nothing.

396
00:14:47,240 --> 00:14:49,560
It is a small slow day in the middle of the week.

397
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:52,380
And Thursday is always better because of it.

398
00:14:53,580 --> 00:14:55,240
A small slow day on Wednesday.

399
00:14:55,940 --> 00:14:57,020
I love that.

400
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:58,620
And it shows something.

401
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:00,440
A slow day is not about time.

402
00:15:01,040 --> 00:15:02,640
It is about permission.

403
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:05,120
You give yourself permission to do nothing.

404
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,760
Even for one hour.

405
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:08,410
And that permission is the hard part.

406
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,220
Permission.

407
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:10,980
Yes, Ben.

408
00:15:11,370 --> 00:15:13,360
Nobody gives us permission.

409
00:15:13,420 --> 00:15:21,860
Our boss does not say, "Please rest." Our phone does not say, "Please stop." So we must say it to ourselves.

410
00:15:23,230 --> 00:15:24,140
"It is okay.

411
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:29,490
You can have a slow day." Everyone listening, you can say it too.

412
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,340
It is okay.

413
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:34,140
It is okay.

414
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:37,060
Okay, so that was part two.

415
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:39,440
Why a slow day is okay.

416
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:42,570
We talked about niksen, the Dutch word for doing nothing.

417
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:46,320
We said the mind works quietly when we rest.

418
00:15:46,380 --> 00:15:48,740
And we said rest is not a reward.

419
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:49,800
It is a part of life.

420
00:15:50,940 --> 00:15:52,360
Now, part three.

421
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:54,180
Simple ideas for a slow day.

422
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,700
Mia, you go first this time.

423
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:59,040
Okay, part three.

424
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:02,180
My first idea is very simple.

425
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:04,600
Put your phone in another room.

426
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:05,600
Not off.

427
00:16:05,660 --> 00:16:06,960
Just in another room.

428
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:10,430
On a slow day, the phone is the biggest enemy.

429
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:13,099
It brings the whole world into your bed.

430
00:16:13,740 --> 00:16:14,099
Work.

431
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:15,060
News.

432
00:16:15,380 --> 00:16:16,940
Other people's busy lives.

433
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,140
So the phone goes to the kitchen.

434
00:16:19,660 --> 00:16:20,860
And I stay in the bedroom.

435
00:16:22,330 --> 00:16:23,810
The phone goes to the kitchen.

436
00:16:24,340 --> 00:16:25,460
That is a good rule, Mia.

437
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:28,350
My first idea is about the morning.

438
00:16:29,240 --> 00:16:30,600
Do not set an alarm.

439
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:33,540
Let your body decide.

440
00:16:33,580 --> 00:16:36,400
On a work day, the alarm is the boss.

441
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:38,680
On a slow day, your body is the boss.

442
00:16:39,540 --> 00:16:42,440
If it wants ten hours of sleep, give it ten hours.

443
00:16:43,740 --> 00:16:44,820
Ten hours.

444
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:47,340
My body would love that, Ben.

445
00:16:48,120 --> 00:16:49,860
My second idea is about food.

446
00:16:50,600 --> 00:16:51,680
Cook something slow.

447
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:53,100
Not fast food.

448
00:16:53,460 --> 00:16:54,500
Not a quick sandwich.

449
00:16:55,020 --> 00:16:56,280
Something that takes time.

450
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:57,300
Soup.

451
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:58,980
Rice with vegetables.

452
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,100
A cake, if you like baking.

453
00:17:01,820 --> 00:17:03,180
The cooking is the rest.

454
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:07,120
You stir, you wait, you smell.

455
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:09,700
Your hands are busy, but your mind is quiet.

456
00:17:10,990 --> 00:17:16,940
"Your hands are busy, but your mind is quiet." Mia, that is exactly niksen.

457
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:19,420
My second idea is smaller.

458
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:22,040
Sit by a window for ten minutes.

459
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:23,540
Just sit.

460
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:24,900
Do not read.

461
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:26,120
Do not scroll.

462
00:17:26,820 --> 00:17:27,540
Look outside.

463
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:31,240
Watch the clouds, or the street, or the rain.

464
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:32,960
Ten minutes.

465
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:34,900
It feels long at first.

466
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:36,720
Then it feels short.

467
00:17:38,260 --> 00:17:39,600
I want to try that today, Ben.

468
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:41,189
Ten minutes at the window.

469
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,100
Do you have a third idea?

470
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:45,200
Yes, Mia.

471
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:46,960
My third idea is about words.

472
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:49,180
Change the words you use.

473
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:56,120
Do not say, "I did nothing today." Say, "I rested today." Same day.

474
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,200
Different words.

475
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:59,400
"Nothing" sounds empty.

476
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:01,700
"Rest" sounds full.

477
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:05,060
And the voice inside us listens to our words.

478
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:08,200
Same day, different words.

479
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:10,260
That is very true, Ben.

480
00:18:10,330 --> 00:18:11,740
Words change how we feel.

481
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:15,120
My third idea is about other people.

482
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:18,990
Tell someone, "Today is my slow day." Your family.

483
00:18:19,420 --> 00:18:20,040
Your friend.

484
00:18:20,330 --> 00:18:21,000
Your roommate.

485
00:18:21,730 --> 00:18:24,560
Then they do not ask, "What are you doing?" They know.

486
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:26,820
And you do not need to explain.

487
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:29,450
And maybe they want a slow day too.

488
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:31,520
And I have a fourth idea, Mia.

489
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:33,620
Do not plan the slow day.

490
00:18:34,260 --> 00:18:35,020
This is important.

491
00:18:35,580 --> 00:18:37,180
Many people make a plan for rest.

492
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,780
"At ten, I read.

493
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:40,400
At eleven, I walk.

494
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:45,660
At twelve, I nap." But then the slow day becomes a work day with different tasks.

495
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:46,940
So no plan.

496
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:50,870
Wake up, and ask, "What do I want now?" And do that.

497
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:52,370
Maybe it is nothing.

498
00:18:52,960 --> 00:18:54,090
Then nothing is the answer.

499
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:58,900
"Then nothing is the answer." Ben, I do that every time.

500
00:18:59,460 --> 00:19:00,760
I write a rest plan.

501
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:01,600
Bath at ten.

502
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:02,860
Book at eleven.

503
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:06,100
And then I feel bad because I am behind on my rest.

504
00:19:06,970 --> 00:19:08,280
That is silly.

505
00:19:08,340 --> 00:19:09,060
Okay.

506
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:09,720
No plan.

507
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:10,840
Just the day.

508
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:12,960
Maybe they want a slow day too.

509
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:14,880
Then you can do nothing together.

510
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:16,920
That is the best kind of nothing.

511
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:19,320
And I have one last idea, Mia.

512
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:22,180
It is for people who cannot have a whole slow day.

513
00:19:22,940 --> 00:19:23,340
Parents.

514
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:24,980
People with two jobs.

515
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:26,720
Students before an exam.

516
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:29,820
For them, a slow day is not possible.

517
00:19:30,420 --> 00:19:32,200
But a slow ten minutes is possible.

518
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:33,360
Yes, Ben.

519
00:19:33,780 --> 00:19:34,640
That is important.

520
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:37,080
Not everyone can have a slow Sunday.

521
00:19:37,700 --> 00:19:39,620
But everyone can have a slow ten minutes.

522
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:41,660
A cup of tea with no phone.

523
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:42,820
A short walk.

524
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:45,860
Sitting in the car for a moment before going inside.

525
00:19:46,380 --> 00:19:48,600
Ten slow minutes inside a fast day.

526
00:19:49,170 --> 00:19:50,460
That is enough.

527
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:51,180
That is enough.

528
00:19:51,870 --> 00:19:53,660
And I think that is our message today, Mia.

529
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,400
A slow day is okay.

530
00:19:56,040 --> 00:19:57,160
A slow hour is okay.

531
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,320
A slow ten minutes is okay.

532
00:20:00,180 --> 00:20:04,480
The voice will say, "You are wasting time." And we can answer, "No.

533
00:20:04,980 --> 00:20:05,600
I am resting.

534
00:20:06,150 --> 00:20:07,080
And rest is okay."

535
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:08,560
Rest is okay.

536
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:14,610
Ben, let's repeat today's important words, slowly, because our listeners want to remember them.

537
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:16,360
Slow.

538
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,160
Not fast.

539
00:20:17,900 --> 00:20:19,040
A slow day.

540
00:20:19,140 --> 00:20:19,840
A slow walk.

541
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:21,600
A slow breakfast.

542
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:22,900
Rest.

543
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,140
To stop and do nothing for a while.

544
00:20:25,820 --> 00:20:26,560
I need rest.

545
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,420
Rest is not a reward.

546
00:20:29,040 --> 00:20:29,320
Okay.

547
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:29,860
Fine.

548
00:20:30,060 --> 00:20:30,540
Good enough.

549
00:20:31,080 --> 00:20:31,760
It is okay.

550
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:33,000
You are okay.

551
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:34,180
Nothing.

552
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:35,460
Not one thing.

553
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:37,840
I did nothing today.

554
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:38,800
A day with nothing.

555
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:39,880
Day.

556
00:20:40,270 --> 00:20:41,220
Twenty-four hours.

557
